Shanti’s Learning World — A fun and interactive learning app for kids ages 2+ featuring ABCs, numbers, colors, shapes, games, and early-learning activities.
Build a fun, colorful, kid-friendly educational learning app called Shanti’s Learning World for children ages 2 and up.

The app should have a cute, welcoming design with a little Black girl character named Shanti wearing a white and pink dress. Make the overall style playful, bright, safe, and easy for toddlers and young children to use.

Include these main learning areas:

* ABC Learning: Teach letters A–Z with pictures, sounds, and simple words.
* 123 Learning: Teach numbers 1–20 with counting activities.
* Colors: Teach basic colors using fun objects and interactive activities.
* Shapes: Teach circles, squares, triangles, rectangles, and other simple shapes.
* Matching Games: Match letters, numbers, colors, and pictures.
* Tracing: Allow children to trace letters and numbers with their finger.
* Mini Games: Add simple educational games with positive encouragement.
* Story Time: Include short, age-appropriate learning stories featuring Shanti.
* Progress: Let parents see basic learning progress and completed activities.

Create a simple home screen with large buttons and icons so a 2-year-old can easily navigate the app. Use encouraging messages such as “Great Job!”, “You Did It!”, and “Keep Learning!”

Make the app responsive so it works well on phones and tablets. Keep the interface simple, colorful, and easy to understand, with large touch-friendly buttons.

The goal is to make learning ABCs, numbers, colors, shapes, and early skills feel like a fun adventure with Shanti.
